d revenue. So you’re absolutely right that it *can* be permanent. The documentary was showing the ideal, the way a great museum would restore a painting and make sure the frame is original, too. The sad reality is that for most movies, the cost of that original frame is so prohibitive that they sell the painting with a cheap new one, hoping the average viewer won’t notice the difference.
